1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:03,143
The Bun Router also doesn't stop at basic

2
00:00:03,159 --> 00:00:04,057
routes like that.

3
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:07,682
You can also register routes that include

4
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:08,981
path parameters

5
00:00:09,558 --> 00:00:12,060
like here where I get some course ID.

6
00:00:12,702 --> 00:00:15,669
This is the syntax for setting up a dynamic

7
00:00:15,733 --> 00:00:18,203
path with the Bun Router. So you're telling

8
00:00:18,235 --> 00:00:21,763
Bun that you got a /courses/some ID route

9
00:00:21,763 --> 00:00:23,672
where you don't know the ID in advance, it

10
00:00:23,672 --> 00:00:24,650
can be different IDs.

11
00:00:25,356 --> 00:00:27,072
And then this handler function here will

12
00:00:27,136 --> 00:00:29,349
become active whenever this route is hit.

13
00:00:30,587 --> 00:00:31,808
So if I save this

14
00:00:32,499 --> 00:00:34,588
and I go to /courses/abc,

15
00:00:35,231 --> 00:00:35,648
you'll see

16
00:00:36,195 --> 00:00:39,087
course ID abc here because that is the

17
00:00:39,103 --> 00:00:42,398
response I am returning here, no fancy HTML

18
00:00:42,398 --> 00:00:44,904
page because of this dynamic route.

19
00:00:45,451 --> 00:00:47,765
So the Bun Router also supports dynamic

20
00:00:47,845 --> 00:00:48,472
routes like this.
